A **marketing channel** is a way through which you reach customers.

| Channel | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Google Search** | Capture people actively searching |
| **Google Maps** | Help local customers find you |
| **Website** | Explain products/services |
| **Instagram** | Awareness & engagement |
| **Facebook** | Local reach |
| **Google Ads** | Paid search traffic |
| **Meta Ads** | Paid social reach |
| **Email** | Retention |
| **WhatsApp** | Enquiries/conversations |

---

# Marketing Objective

A **marketing objective** is what you're trying to achieve.

---

# KPI

**KPI = Key Performance Indicator**

These are measurements that tell us whether our marketing is working.

---

# Vanity Metrics

A **vanity metric** looks impressive but may not mean much for the business.

**Attention is not the same as business results.**

---

# Example Marketing Plan

**Goal:** More store visits

**Customer:** Local homeowners / electricians / contractors

**Channel:** Google Search + Google Maps

**Message:** Relevant electrical/hardware products available locally

**Action:** Call / Directions / Visit

**Measurement:** Calls, enquiries, directions, visits/sales where measurable

**Optimization:** Improve keywords, ads, website, profile, targeting, etc.

